## What belongs in a closure record

A reviewer six months from now should be able to reproduce your conclusion without asking you. Attach the following to every closed ticket:

- the finding identifier, asset name and IP address;
- the date and time of the fix and of the verification;
- the scan policy, scanner version and plugin feed date;
- the before and after output, trimmed to the relevant lines;
- the name of the person who verified, if different from the fixer.

Store this in the ticket itself, not in a personal folder. Auditors and incident responders will later use it to learn exactly when a system became safe, and whether it was ever unsafe in between.
